          "author": "jcfp",
          "author_is_release_team": false,
          "content": "## FFE ##\n\n[Rationale]\n\n* Upstream micro-releases 5.1.2 and 5.1.3 fix multiple serious security issues. See the developers' summary at https://sabnzbd.org/wiki/extra/5.1-vulnerabilities.html\n\n[ Scope ]\n\n* Security fixes and related changes to the upstream testsuite only. The sabnzbdplus package has no reverse dependencies.\n\n* $ seeded-in-ubuntu sabnzbdplus\n  sabnzbdplus's binaries are not seeded.\n\n* Diff of the upstream changelog since the version included in the archive is attached in changelog.diff.\n\n[ Regression Potential ]\n\n* Low. Targeted upstream changes only, no significant packaging changes. Version 5.1.3 has been packaged in Debian for over two weeks, as well as on my PPA (ppa:jcfp/ppa resp. ppa:jcfp/nobetas) which is advertised upstream, with no issues reported. There are no API changes and no changes in the package's dependencies. The sabnzbdplus package has no reverse dependencies.\n\n[ Testing ]\n\n* Smoke test:\n  - PPA: https://launchpad.net/~jcfp/+archive/ubuntu/private/+sourcepub/18806883/+listing-archive-extra\n  - Build: https://launchpad.net/~jcfp/+archive/ubuntu/private/+build/33802500/+files/buildlog_ubuntu-stonking-amd64.sabnzbdplus_5.1.3+dfsg-1ubuntu1_BUILDING.txt.gz\n  - Installation: https://paste.debian.net/hidden/97c894c3\n  - Upgrade: https://paste.debian.net/hidden/94ca2b86\n  - Autopkgtest: https://ci.debian.net/data/autopkgtest/testing/amd64/s/sabnzbdplus/76162808/log.gz\n  - Does it break other packages: nope",
